Important notes on setting this game up:The save files are all saved in the same directory, which is ownedby the same account that owns the game.  This is for preventingcheaters (save + copy).  For this reason the game is mode 4111, set uidon execution.  Any files and directories associated with the game shouldonly read + write to the owner.			This game has no implied warrantee, 			I have it running on BSD 4.4c.Any problems sent to me will be looked at, but I cannot Gaurantee thatI will be able to respond.  (This is my last semester).  This game is the result of my senior project, (1 semester course, due to time considerationsthis game may be a little inefficient in places).				~Ted Wisniewski				(The Wizard)===============================================I had to make several changes to get this game to compile, plus severalothers to get it to run. I have a hard time believing it ever worked. Itried contacting the author, but got no reply. The source, as it ishere, compiles and runs OK on a Sun 3/60 SunOS 3.5; I make nogaurantees beyond that.	-Bill Randle	Moderator, comp.sources.games	Tektronix, Inc.	games@saab.CNA.TEK.COM	Feb. 22, 1990